  "output": "The book follows a magitech artificer who possesses the ability to secretly feel the \"deep, forbidden Facets of magic\" [1]. The story involves the protagonist taking a routine guild job in a ruin that is \"folded out of space and stuck in a single looping hour\" [1]. The narrative structure includes a \"Commission\" where a party takes the \"Nine\" and finds it is wrong, followed by a section focused on \"the loop, the survivor, the Keystone, and the choice\" [3].\n\nThe protagonist is **Cael Ferren**, a 26-year-old brass-rank artificer [2, 5]. She has spent her life hiding her ability to feel the deep Facets, believing the \"hum\" she experiences is a \"sickness the Wardens are right to cut out\" [5]. Her goal is to maintain a \"quiet, paid, unremarkable career at the Commission Hall,\" but she eventually learns that the hum is actually \"the last true compass to a magic the world broke on purpose\" [5].",
